# Where the browser sends its requests in ANY production-mode build.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Vite fills `import.meta.env.VITE_*` from .env files
# read out of `envDir`, NOT from the shell environment. A deploy script can
# `export VITE_ACCOUNT_URL=/auth` all it likes: unless an app's vite.config
# also copies process.env into a `define` block -- and only one of the four
# does -- the build sees nothing and compiles its own fallback instead. Those
# fallbacks are `http://localhost:<port>`, so production shipped a site whose
# Join form posted to the visitor's own machine and reported "Could not reach
# C7 right now" while the server answered 201 to the identical request.
#
# Staging had been working on a hand-written /srv/videofy/app/.env that existed
# on exactly one machine and in no repository. This file replaces that: every
# production-mode build, on any box or laptop, gets the same answer.
#
# PATHS, NOT ORIGINS. Every surface is served from the origin the page is
# already on, so one set of values is correct for staging and production alike
# and no build has to know which one it is. It also means a bundle copied
# between environments cannot address the wrong one.
#
# `vite dev` runs in development mode and does not read this file, so local
# work keeps its localhost defaults.

VITE_GATEWAY_URL=/
VITE_ACCOUNT_URL=/auth
VITE_INGEST_URL=/media
VITE_CALL_PATH=/call/
VITE_VIEWER_BASE=/listen
VITE_PROGRESSIVE_TRANSLATED_AUDIO=true
